    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ87eBplA",
      "title": "[codex] fix(proxyd): bump optimism dependencies",
      "author": "karlfloersch",
      "number": 628,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nBumps proxyd's Optimism dependency to `v1.18.2-0.20260521143954-7657968676a2` and updates the matching op-geth replace to `v1.101702.3-rc.1`.\n\nThis also applies the mechanical access-list helper import updates required by the newer Optimism module: those helpers now live under `op-core/interop/messages` instead of `op-supervisor/supervisor/types`.\n\n## Notes\n\nI tried the current Optimism `develop` tip `e7c16a1fd92f999807c668a1842fbb59fbb315ee` from May 21, 2026, but Go's checksum database does not have that pseudo-version available yet. This PR uses `7657968676a209f44ed3a845cc56c52a79232032`, which includes the merged op-service interop filter client.\n\nThis PR intentionally does not change proxyd's interop RPC behavior; it is only the dependency bump plus compile-required type moves.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test . -count=1`\n- `go test ./integration_tests -run TestInteropValidation_NormalFlow -count=1 -timeout=180s -v`\n- `go test ./... -count=1 -timeout=10m`\n- after rebasing onto latest `main`: `go test . -count=1`\n- after rebasing onto latest `main`: `go test ./integration_tests -run TestInteropValidation_NormalFlow -count=1 -timeout=180s`",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-21T16:42:59Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 126,
      "deletions": 104
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ87eDYe6",
      "title": "[codex] test(proxyd): wait for websocket close handler",
      "author": "karlfloersch",
      "number": 630,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nStabilizes `TestWSClientExceedReadLimit` by waiting for the websocket close handler to run instead of checking a boolean immediately after `WriteMessage` returns.\n\n## Why\n\nAfter #626 fixed CircleCI path filtering and let proxyd tests run again, both stacked proxyd PRs failed in this test at `ws_test.go:239`. The oversized write can return an error before the close handler callback runs, so the old assertion was timing-sensitive.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test ./integration_tests -run TestWSClientExceedReadLimit -count=1 -v`",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-21T18:07:37Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 10,
      "deletions": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ87eDA36",
      "title": "[codex] ci: use supported Python for path filtering",
      "author": "karlfloersch",
      "number": 629,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nSets the CircleCI `path-filtering/filter` job image tag to `3.10`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe setup job currently resolves to `cimg/python:3.9` and downloads the latest `get-pip.py`, which now exits with:\n\n```\nERROR: This script does not work on Python 3.9. The minimum supported Python version is 3.10.\n```\n\nThe `circleci/path-filtering@1.3.0` orb supports the `tag` parameter for choosing the Python image tag, so this keeps the existing orb and only moves the setup job to a supported Python runtime.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Existing failing CircleCI job: `check-updated-files` failed before continuation while running `get-pip.py` on Python 3.9.\n- This PR is expected to validate through CircleCI because it changes the setup job runtime itself.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-21T17:48:52Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 1,
      "deletions": 0
    }
  ],
